# Sep 3 2026: this project had no real .gitignore anywhere -- confirmed
# both by inspecting the live public repo directly and by the 5 local
# .gitignore files uploaded here, every one of which was empty except
# for the single line "!.gitignore" (a placeholder, never real rules).
# This is why backend/venv (486MB), frontend/node_modules (124MB),
# backend/.env, backend/db.sqlite3, and the log files all ended up
# committed. One root-level file, not one per folder -- git applies
# these path patterns from wherever this file sits, so backend/ and
# frontend/ don't each need their own copy.

# --- Secrets -- never commit real credentials ---
.env
backend/.env
*.env
!.env.example
!backend/.env.example

# --- Python / Django ---
venv/
backend/venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.sqlite3
db.sqlite3
backend/db.sqlite3
*.log
backend/*.log

# --- Node / React / Vite ---
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
dist/
frontend/dist/
.vite/

# --- OS/editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- This project's own generated/runtime data --
# (signal_logs and fundamentals_data.json are real trading history and
# fundamentals cache this project generates as it runs -- excluded
# since regenerated data doesn't belong in source control the same way
# actual code does. Uncomment the next two lines if you want them
# tracked instead -- that's a real choice, not a mistake either way.)
# backend/signal_logs/
# backend/fundamentals_data.json
